From: Roy Klopper <roy.klopper@stealthscale.io>
Subject: [PATCH] bash-engine: keep the helpers working under set -u

The helpers expand ${BASH_SOURCE} in PS4 and in the DEBUG trap. At the top
level of `bash -c`, BASH_SOURCE is unset, so a traced child that runs with
`set -u` fails on its first command with "BASH_SOURCE: unbound variable".
A test suite that starts such children then fails only under kcov.

Expanding with a default keeps the marker format and makes the helpers
indifferent to nounset.
---
 src/engines/bash-helper-debug-trap.sh | 2 +-
 src/engines/bash-helper.sh            | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/engines/bash-helper-debug-trap.sh b/src/engines/bash-helper-debug-trap.sh
--- a/src/engines/bash-helper-debug-trap.sh
+++ b/src/engines/bash-helper-debug-trap.sh
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 #!/bin/sh
 
 set -o functrace
-trap 'echo "kcov@${BASH_SOURCE}@${LINENO}@" >&$KCOV_BASH_XTRACEFD' DEBUG
+trap 'echo "kcov@${BASH_SOURCE-}@${LINENO}@" >&$KCOV_BASH_XTRACEFD' DEBUG
 unset BASH_ENV
diff --git a/src/engines/bash-helper.sh b/src/engines/bash-helper.sh
--- a/src/engines/bash-helper.sh
+++ b/src/engines/bash-helper.sh
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 #!/bin/sh
 
 # Set PS4, the sh -x prompt.
-PS4='kcov@${BASH_SOURCE}@${LINENO}@'
+PS4='kcov@${BASH_SOURCE-}@${LINENO}@'
 
 # Turn on tracing
 set -x
